cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "frankwolfe-active-set-lookup"
abstract: >-
  A measurement of whether hashing the active set beats a linear scan in
  FrankWolfe.jl, which is the open question of its issue #244 and has stood
  unanswered since 2021. The lookup is exact rather than approximate, so hashing
  is sound; the cost is one scan of the active set per iteration, and it is
  reached from the blended pairwise algorithm but not from away-step Frank-Wolfe,
  which supplies the index itself. Whether that costs anything is an empirical
  question about how large the active set actually grows, and this repository
  answers it with a profile before proposing any change upstream.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-24"
